  "method": "One-off pywin32 COM script. (a) COM states: new workbook, wb.Protect(Password, Structure, Windows) for s1 Structure=True Windows=True no password, s2 same with password 'a', s3 Structure=False Windows=True; SaveAs .xlsx(51)/.xlsb(50). (b) Hand-authored: an empty workbook saved by this Excel as base, then python zipfile rewrote xl/workbook.xml inserting one <workbookProtection .../> element immediately before <bookViews> (where Excel itself writes it, after xr:revisionPtr; inserting right after <workbookPr/> made Workbooks.Open fail); kept as *.input.xlsx. Each input opened in Excel (Workbooks.Open) and SaveAs .xlsx/.xlsb. Survival: workbookProtection element parsed from the saved .xlsx workbook.xml, and ProtectStructure/ProtectWindows read via COM on the open input and on each saved file reopened.",
